WEBVTT

00:00.180 --> 00:04.080
MovingVLA gives mobile agents task and scene memory.

00:06.130 --> 00:09.338
The robot lifts a loaded bowl from the prep island.

00:10.130 --> 00:15.790
For the next step, the agent retrieves stored views
of refrigerator 274.

00:16.120 --> 00:20.268
For this replay, we select a head-on approach to the
refrigerator.

00:21.130 --> 00:25.360
The occupancy map shows free, occupied, and unknown
space.

00:25.580 --> 00:28.668
A-star finds a path to a reachable approach.

00:29.050 --> 00:34.188
As the robot moves past the island, the refrigerator
stays marked on the map.

00:35.000 --> 00:39.578
The green line traces where the robot actually moves
as it carries the bowl.

00:42.160 --> 00:47.390
The frozen Awomo policy uses fresh camera images to
place the bowl on the refrigerator shelf.

00:52.170 --> 00:54.670
Same kitchen. Same starting pose.

00:55.100 --> 00:59.588
The white circle marks the shared start. The diamond
marks the dining counter.

01:09.840 --> 01:12.040
Awomo returns near its start.

01:12.190 --> 01:14.420
HarnessVLA turns back.

01:14.560 --> 01:16.850
MovingVLA delivers the basket.

01:17.140 --> 01:23.830
Expert demonstrations teach the task order. Scene
memory grounds each step in a specific object and the
space around it.

01:24.650 --> 01:29.848
These BEHAVIOR-1K rollouts show three tasks from the
R1Pro’s head camera.

01:44.650 --> 01:50.138
Four recordings show the physical CRUZR S2 moving
objects between workstations.
